The cumulative probability at the change of density is $F(3)=3\times\frac1{12}=\frac14$. Since $\frac14<\frac12$, the median lies in the second interval.
For $3\le x\le6$, accumulate the probability from the first interval before integrating the second.
$\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\frac14+\int_3^x\frac14\,dt\\&=\frac14+\frac{x-3}{4}\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\frac14+\frac{m-3}{4}&=\frac12\\m-3&=1\\m&=4\end{aligned}$
The value $4$ lies in the second interval.
