examples.question_text:
The cumulative frequency polygon shows the heights of $80$ plants. Estimate the interquartile range, correct to two decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=75mm,height=60mm,axis lines=left,xlabel={Height (cm)},ylabel={Cumulative frequency},xmin=0,xmax=52,ymin=0,ymax=84,xtick={0,10,20,30,40,50},ytick={0,10,20,30,40,50,60,70,80},grid=major,grid style={draw=housegrid},axis line style={black},tick style={black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\addplot[mathblue,thick] coordinates {(0,0) (10,8) (20,32) (30,56) (40,72) (50,80)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The total frequency is $80$. Read $Q_1$ at cumulative frequency $20$ and $Q_3$ at cumulative frequency $60$.
On the straight segment from $(10,8)$ to $(20,32)$:
$\begin{aligned}Q_1&=10+\frac{20-8}{32-8}(20-10)\\&=15\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$
On the straight segment from $(30,56)$ to $(40,72)$:
$\begin{aligned}Q_3&=30+\frac{60-56}{72-56}(40-30)\\&=32.5\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\text{IQR}&=Q_3-Q_1\\&=32.5-15\\&=17.50\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$
